{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"A U.S. ETF seeking relief beyond Rule 6c-11 generally files an exemptive application with the SEC under Investment Company Act § 6(c), explaining the requested relief and supporting facts. The SEC publishes a notice of the application in the Federal Register, inviting interested persons to request a hearing; absent a hearing request, it may issue an order granting relief after the notice period. The order—not the filing or notice—provides the requested exemption.\n\nRule 0-5 expedited review is available only if the application meets the rule’s conditions, including use of the required structured format and representations that the requested relief is substantially identical to relief previously granted and raises no novel issues. The 45-day period runs from publication of the notice, not filing, and is a target for SEC action (grant or denial), subject to extension or removal from expedited review—not a guaranteed approval deadline."}}
